  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday Night through Wednesday)\nIssued at 1145 PM CDT Wed Jul 22 2026\n\nA stronger mid level wave will round the top of the ridge and drop\ninto the Central Plains Friday morning and progress southeastward\nthrough the afternoon hours as the ridge retrogrades westward a\nbit. The result will again be increasing cloud cover and at least\nlow to moderate rain chances over much of eastern Oklahoma and\nnorthwest Arkansas. The trough axis remains in the region through\nSaturday morning with scattered showers and isolated thunderstorms\ncontinuing through this period. Rain amounts generally look to be\nlight for most locations with some locally heavier amounts\npossible within any thunderstorms. Southerly winds return on \nFriday as well with dewpoints increasing, pushing heat indices \nback near headline criteria Friday afternoon and especially by \nSaturday as temperatures begin to warm above normal again.\n\nUpper ridging builds back into the region in the wake of the\nexiting shortwave this weekend. Hot and humid conditions will once\nagain return through the rest of the forecast period, with very\nlimited rain chances through much of next week. Triple digit\ntemperatures become more likely areawide by Sunday through mid \nweek, with heat headlines likely needed through the rest of the\nforecast period. Ridging could then shift westward again by late \nweek allowing some slight relief to the heat and low rain chances \nto return to parts of the area.\n\nBowlan",
